# Integrity

Do not tune on the test set. The probe split is the gate's only acceptance signal.

Record every analytical finding and every visual finding before the session ends.

Analytical record, in the ledger: step metrics, diagnostics, every edit proposal, every gate decision (accepted and rejected), lineage, and a `findings` row. Kinds are `observation`, `negative`, `claim`, and `method`. Failed seeds and negative results stay. Also write the narrative in `docs/09_JOURNAL.md`.

Visual record: Plotly for exploration, matplotlib or seaborn for the paper, Okabe-Ito palette. Each paper figure is exported by a notebook cell with a provenance manifest (git commit, config hash, seeds, ledger version, ledger hashes, device). The finding row's `evidence_ref` points at that manifest. Title synthetic figures `SYNTHETIC`. `assert_citable` rejects them.

A claim in docs or in `paper/` names a manifest whose `synthetic` field is false. A number with no manifest is not a result.

Citations are sources opened in this session. If the PDF was not opened, say so and leave it off `paper/refs.bib`.

`assert_same_machine` before any pooled table. CUDA and MPS results stay in separate tables.

Hypotheses live in `docs/01_RESEARCH_QUESTIONS.md`. Edit them only with an ADR written before the confirmatory run.
